1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,126
Your battery percentage is a guess.

2
00:00:02,176 --> 00:00:04,343
Here's how your phone makes it.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,943
There's no way to see inside a battery,

4
00:00:06,943 --> 00:00:09,340
so a tiny chip, called a fuel gauge,

5
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:10,850
watches it instead.

6
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,239
First, it counts every bit of charge flowing

7
00:00:13,239 --> 00:00:14,070
in and out.

8
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:15,984
But tiny counting errors pile up

9
00:00:15,984 --> 00:00:16,850
over time.

10
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,350
So it also checks the voltage.

11
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:20,150
The catch?

12
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:21,390
Through the middle of the charge,

13
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:23,350
the voltage barely moves.

14
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,140
So the chip blends both,

15
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:27,140
using a model of your battery:

16
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:28,611
its temperature, its age,

17
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:30,350
and how hard you're pushing it.

18
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,870
When reality disagrees,

19
00:00:31,870 --> 00:00:33,350
it corrects the guess.

20
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,670
That's how 15% can turn into 3% in a

21
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:39,661
minute, or a cold phone can die at 30%.

22
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,270
And 0% isn't empty.

23
00:00:42,270 --> 00:00:43,392
It's where your phone stops,

24
00:00:43,392 --> 00:00:45,350
to protect the battery.

25
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:47,420
So that number isn't a measurement.

26
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:49,350
It's a very good guess.

27
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:50,620
Send this to the friend who

28
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:52,388
lives at 1%.
